# The variables this app reads at runtime on the VPS. Names only; never put values here.
# Each one needs two things:
#   - a repo secret (or, if it isn't secret, a repo variable) named ENV_<NAME>, and
#   - a matching line in the "Write .env" step of .github/workflows/build-and-deploy.yml.
# ENV_POSTGRES_PASSWORD below becomes POSTGRES_PASSWORD in the .env the deploy writes on the VPS.

# Required. Password of the database's moodle user (secret). Letters and digits only. Postgres only reads it
# when the db-data volume is first created, so changing it later locks Moodle out of its database.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# Required. The password of Moodle's admin account (secret). Only read when Moodle is installed into an
# empty database; after that, change it in Moodle. At least 8 characters with a digit, a lower-case and an
# upper-case letter, and a symbol other than a single quote.
MOODLE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Required. The admin account's email address (variable). Only read at install, like the password.
MOODLE_ADMIN_EMAIL=
